{
  "_doc": "The one list of event kinds, link kinds and sample metrics of ie-run/3. A kind's code is its position in kinds (stable across runs). tier = rank 0 (coarsest) to 6; stepping at tier r visits every row with tier <= r. nest_bump: a row whose parent has the same kind is one tier finer, one step only (nested NVTX = op). derived: rows the importer calculates (no source row). home: the scene level that draws the kind first. link_kinds with cause=true fill the cause column of the link's target row (one origin per row) instead of the browser's links block. metrics: the sample metric catalog. sidebar=true puts a metric in the hardware sidebar; source and period_ms (null until measured) are its evidence, and each run's manifest adds the measured period of its samples. A metric not listed is in the catalog with sidebar=false. The nvml group is written by the step-5 live sampler (backend/store/nvml.py): clock names the sampler group whose reads share one timestamp (one samples block per clock), and period_ms is the polling period chosen from the measured refresh table /mnt/ie-data/cc/probe/nvml_refresh.json (backend/store/probe_nvml.py); store-check fails when they differ. evidence (optional) replaces the sample group's evidence for one metric (GPM: the measured lag). The docker group is the Docker Engine stats stream per container (one clock per container); the engine group is the engine's Prometheus scrape (1 Hz): series names the Prometheus base name, summed over its label sets, histogram buckets not kept. Adding a kind is one entry here; a kind not listed stops the import. ladders: the tiers of each dimension of the command center, coarse to fine (COMMAND_CENTER.md section 3). place: where a kind sits in each dimension: a ladder tier, \"detail\" (never a stop) or \"-\" (no place in that dimension), with what it lands on in brackets. A rule {if, then, else} picks per row: \"top-level\" (not nested in its own kind), \"launch\" (the cause of a kernel, memcpy or memset row: the CPU side of that kernel stop), \"module forward\" (the name matches \"match\"), \"profiled\" (the kernel has Nsight Compute counters). design/dimensions/stop_counts.py applies it; the importer and the browser do not read it yet (P3).",
  "tiers": ["request", "iteration", "stage", "op", "call", "device", "os"],
  "levels": ["Infrastructure", "Components", "Trace", "Iteration", "Model ops", "Kernel", "Hardware"],
  "ladders": {"execution": ["request", "iteration", "phase", "layer", "module", "kernel"],
              "hardware": ["system", "node", "device", "unit", "kernel traffic", "SM internals"],
              "architecture": ["fleet", "node", "container", "process", "component", "software layer"]},
  "kinds": [
    {"kind": "client request",       "tier": 0, "color": "#d08770", "label": "request",          "home": "Trace",
     "place": {"execution": "request", "hardware": "-", "architecture": "component (client boxes)"}},
    {"kind": "container event",      "tier": 0, "color": "#ebcb8b", "label": "container event",  "home": "Infrastructure",
     "place": {"execution": "detail", "hardware": "-", "architecture": "container (lifecycle stop)"}},
    {"kind": "iteration",            "tier": 1, "color": "#a3be8c", "label": "iteration",        "home": "Iteration", "derived": true,
     "place": {"execution": "iteration", "hardware": "-", "architecture": "component (worker)"}},
    {"kind": "engine timestamp",     "tier": 1, "color": "#a3be8c", "label": "engine timestamp", "home": "Trace",
     "place": {"execution": "detail (of its request)", "hardware": "-", "architecture": "component (worker)"}},
    {"kind": "component stamp",      "tier": 2, "color": "#88c0d0", "label": "stamp",            "home": "Components",
     "place": {"execution": "phase", "hardware": "-", "architecture": "component"}},
    {"kind": "client event",         "tier": 2, "color": "#d08770", "label": "client event",     "home": "Components",
     "place": {"execution": "phase", "hardware": "-", "architecture": "component (client)"}},
    {"kind": "client transport",     "tier": 2, "color": "#d08770", "label": "transport",        "home": "Components",
     "place": {"execution": "phase", "hardware": "-", "architecture": "component (client transport)"}},
    {"kind": "network frame",        "tier": 2, "color": "#ebcb8b", "label": "frame",            "home": "Components",
     "place": {"execution": "phase", "hardware": "device (NIC link)", "architecture": "container (network)"}},
    {"kind": "nvtx range",           "tier": 2, "color": "#5e6b7d", "label": "NVTX range",       "home": "Iteration", "nest_bump": true,
     "place": {"execution": {"if": "top-level", "then": "phase", "else": "detail"}, "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "component (worker)"}},
    {"kind": "cuda graph node",      "tier": 3, "color": "#4c6faf", "label": "graph node",       "home": "Model ops",
     "place": {"execution": "detail", "hardware": "device (GPU)", "architecture": "software layer (runtime)"}},
    {"kind": "cuda runtime call",    "tier": 4, "color": "#3a9c6a", "label": "CUDA call",        "home": "Model ops",
     "place": {"execution": {"if": "launch", "then": "kernel (CPU side)", "else": "detail"}, "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "software layer (runtime)"}},
    {"kind": "cuda driver call",     "tier": 4, "color": "#3a9c6a", "label": "CUDA driver call", "home": "Model ops",
     "place": {"execution": {"if": "launch", "then": "kernel (CPU side)", "else": "detail"}, "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "software layer (runtime)"}},
    {"kind": "cuda synchronization", "tier": 4, "color": "#3a9c6a", "label": "CUDA sync",        "home": "Model ops",
     "place": {"execution": "detail", "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "software layer (runtime)"}},
    {"kind": "cuda event record",    "tier": 4, "color": "#3a9c6a", "label": "CUDA event",       "home": "Model ops",
     "place": {"execution": "detail", "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "software layer (runtime)"}},
    {"kind": "cpu operator",         "tier": 4, "color": "#b48ead", "label": "CPU operator",     "home": "Model ops",
     "place": {"execution": "detail (under its module)", "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "software layer (toolkit)"}},
    {"kind": "python call",          "tier": 4, "color": "#5e81ac", "label": "Python call",      "home": "Trace",
     "place": {"execution": {"if": "module forward", "match": "^tensorrt_llm/_torch/(modules|attention_backend|distributed)/[^()]+\\(\\d+\\): forward$", "then": "module", "else": "detail"}, "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "software layer (toolkit)"}},
    {"kind": "kernel",               "tier": 5, "color": "#2457c5", "label": "kernel",           "home": "Kernel",
     "place": {"execution": "kernel", "hardware": {"if": "profiled", "then": "kernel traffic", "else": "unit (SMs)"}, "architecture": "software layer (device code)"}},
    {"kind": "memcpy",               "tier": 5, "color": "#c2507a", "label": "memcpy",           "home": "Model ops",
     "place": {"execution": "kernel", "hardware": "device (PCIe link, copy engine)", "architecture": "software layer (device code)"}},
    {"kind": "memset",               "tier": 5, "color": "#8a8f98", "label": "memset",           "home": "Model ops",
     "place": {"execution": "kernel", "hardware": "unit (copy engine, VRAM)", "architecture": "software layer (device code)"}},
    {"kind": "os runtime call",      "tier": 6, "color": "#434c5e", "label": "OS call",          "home": "Trace",
     "place": {"execution": "detail", "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "process (OS)"}},
    {"kind": "profiler overhead",    "tier": 6, "color": "#434c5e", "label": "profiler",         "home": "Trace",
     "place": {"execution": "detail", "hardware": "device (CPU)", "architecture": "process (profiler)"}},
    {"kind": "profiler message",     "tier": 6, "color": "#434c5e", "label": "profiler",         "home": "Trace",
     "place": {"execution": "detail", "hardware": "-", "architecture": "process (profiler)"}}
  ],
  "link_kinds": [
    {"kind": "cuda launch", "cause": true,  "label": "launch"},
    {"kind": "zmq",         "cause": true,  "label": "ZMQ message"},
    {"kind": "network",     "cause": true,  "label": "network message"},
    {"kind": "serves",      "cause": false, "label": "iteration share"}
  ],
  "metrics": [
    {"metric": "nvml.gpm.sm_util",       "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-gpm",     "unit": "%",    "sidebar": true, "label": "SM utilization",       "source": "NVML GPM", "period_ms": 100, "evidence": "Observed: NVML GPM (nvidia-ml-py) between two GPM samples, read by the devtools backend (store/nvml.py); timestamp = CLOCK_MONOTONIC at the read's return; the values describe about 165 ms before the read (measured against nsys GPU metrics on one run, 2026-11-08; the read time is kept, owner 2026-11-08); reads with an empty, zero or under-50 ms window are dropped"},
    {"metric": "nvml.gpm.sm_occupancy",  "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-gpm",     "unit": "%",    "sidebar": true, "label": "SM occupancy",         "source": "NVML GPM", "period_ms": 100, "evidence": "Observed: NVML GPM (nvidia-ml-py) between two GPM samples, read by the devtools backend (store/nvml.py); timestamp = CLOCK_MONOTONIC at the read's return; the values describe about 165 ms before the read (measured against nsys GPU metrics on one run, 2026-11-08; the read time is kept, owner 2026-11-08); reads with an empty, zero or under-50 ms window are dropped"},
    {"metric": "nvml.gpm.tensor_util",   "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-gpm",     "unit": "%",    "sidebar": true, "label": "tensor utilization",   "source": "NVML GPM", "period_ms": 100, "evidence": "Observed: NVML GPM (nvidia-ml-py) between two GPM samples, read by the devtools backend (store/nvml.py); timestamp = CLOCK_MONOTONIC at the read's return; the values describe about 165 ms before the read (measured against nsys GPU metrics on one run, 2026-11-08; the read time is kept, owner 2026-11-08); reads with an empty, zero or under-50 ms window are dropped"},
    {"metric": "nvml.gpm.dram_bw_util",  "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-gpm",     "unit": "%",    "sidebar": true, "label": "DRAM bandwidth",       "source": "NVML GPM", "period_ms": 100, "evidence": "Observed: NVML GPM (nvidia-ml-py) between two GPM samples, read by the devtools backend (store/nvml.py); timestamp = CLOCK_MONOTONIC at the read's return; the values describe about 165 ms before the read (measured against nsys GPU metrics on one run, 2026-11-08; the read time is kept, owner 2026-11-08); reads with an empty, zero or under-50 ms window are dropped"},
    {"metric": "nvml.memory.used",       "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-50ms",    "unit": "MiB",  "sidebar": true, "label": "GPU memory used",      "source": "NVML", "period_ms": 50},
    {"metric": "nvml.power.draw",        "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-500ms",   "unit": "W",    "sidebar": true, "label": "power",                "source": "NVML", "period_ms": 500},
    {"metric": "nvml.clocks.sm",         "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-500ms",   "unit": "MHz",  "sidebar": true, "label": "SM clock",             "source": "NVML", "period_ms": 500},
    {"metric": "nvml.pcie.rx",           "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-pcie-rx", "unit": "KB/s", "sidebar": true, "label": "PCIe RX",              "source": "NVML", "period_ms": 30},
    {"metric": "nvml.pcie.tx",           "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-pcie-tx", "unit": "KB/s", "sidebar": true, "label": "PCIe TX",              "source": "NVML", "period_ms": 30},
    {"metric": "nvml.temperature.gpu",   "group": "nvml", "clock": "nvml-500ms",   "unit": "°C",   "sidebar": true, "label": "GPU temperature",      "source": "NVML", "period_ms": 500},
    {"metric": "utilization.gpu",                      "sidebar": true, "label": "GPU utilization",               "source": "nvidia-smi query (gpu.csv)", "period_ms": 100},
